    "updated_at": "2024-04-04T21:38:54Z",
    "body": "loading=\"idle\" wouldn't probably work too well, since there is often plenty of idle time also during page load. (And I wouldn't want \"idle\" have different meaning with loading attribute)\r\nloading=\"domcontentloaded\" might be also problematic. Many of the resources are often loaded after domcontentloaded. \r\n\r\nThe document yoav linked has some initial ideas how to solve this, but I think those might be overly complicated. And there is the nice todo comment there \"think about images\" :) ",
